  Metadata: {'document_id': 2, 'chunk_index': 0, 'chunk_text': "Financial Policy Document Expense Reimbursement Employees may be reimbursed for business-related expenses incurred while performing their job duties. All expense reports must be submitted within 30 days of the expense and must include: \x7f Original receipts \x7f Business purpose description \x7f Date and location of expense \x7f Amount and currency Travel Expenses \x7f Airfare: Economy class unless business class is approved in advance \x7f Accommodation: Up to $150 per night for domestic travel, $200 for international \x7f Meals: Up to $50 per day for domestic travel, $75 for international \x7f Ground transportation: Actual cost up to $30 per day Client Entertainment Client entertainment expenses must be pre-approved and are limited to $100 per person per event. Budget Approval Process All departmental budgets must be approved by the Finance Department. Budget requests should include: \x7f Detailed breakdown of expenses \x7f Justification for each expense \x7f Timeline for expenditure \x7f Expected return on investment Procurement Policy All purchases over $500 require at least three competitive quotes. Purchases over $5,000 require formal approval from the Finance Department. Invoice Processing Invoices should be submitted to the Finance Department with the following information: \x7f Vendor name and contact information \x7f Invoice number and date \x7f Detailed description of goods or services \x7f Total amount and payment terms \x7f Purchase order number (if applicable) Financial Reporting Monthly financial reports are due on the 15th of each month for the previous month. Department managers are responsible for reviewing and approving their department's financial reports. Contact Information For finance-related questions, please contact the Finance Department at finance@company.com or extension 5678.", 'filename': 'Financial_Policy.pdf', 'intent': 'Finance'}

