Financial Policy Document
 
Expense Reimbursement
Employees may be reimbursed for business-related expenses incurred while performing their job
duties. All expense reports must be submitted within 30 days of the expense and must include:
 Original receipts
 Business purpose description
 Date and location of expense
 Amount and currency
Travel Expenses
 Airfare: Economy class unless business class is approved in advance
 Accommodation: Up to $150 per night for domestic travel, $200 for international
 Meals: Up to $50 per day for domestic travel, $75 for international
 Ground transportation: Actual cost up to $30 per day
Client Entertainment
Client entertainment expenses must be pre-approved and are limited to $100 per person per event.
Budget Approval Process
All departmental budgets must be approved by the Finance Department. Budget requests should
include:
 Detailed breakdown of expenses
 Justification for each expense
 Timeline for expenditure
 Expected return on investment
Procurement Policy
All purchases over $500 require at least three competitive quotes. Purchases over $5,000 require
formal approval from the Finance Department.
Invoice Processing
Invoices should be submitted to the Finance Department with the following information:

 Vendor name and contact information
 Invoice number and date
 Detailed description of goods or services
 Total amount and payment terms
 Purchase order number (if applicable)
Financial Reporting
Monthly financial reports are due on the 15th of each month for the previous month. Department
managers are responsible for reviewing and approving their department's financial reports.
Contact Information
For finance-related questions, please contact the Finance Department at finance@company.com or
extension 5678.



